<i data-commentator="Ateret Zekenim" data-label="♦" data-order="4"></i><i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ו" data-order="6"></i>It is good<i data-commentator="Turei Zahav" data-order="4"></i><i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="9"></i><i data-commentator="Mishnah Berurah" data-label="יג"></i>to' <i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="7"></i>recite the Binding of Isaac,<i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ז" data-order="7"></i>the passage of the manna,<i data-commentator="Be'er HaGolah" data-label="ח" data-order="8"></i>the Ten<i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="8"></i>Commandments, and the passages<i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="10"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="10"></i><i data-commentator="Mishnah Berurah" data-label="יד"></i>of olah, minchah,<i data-commentator="Eshel Avraham" data-label="ב" data-order="2"></i><i data-commentator="Mishnah Berurah" data-label="טו"></i>shelamim, chatat, and asham.<small>Specifically<i data-commentator="Turei Zahav" data-order="5"></i>as an individual one may recite the Ten Commandments every day, but it is forbidden to recite them with<i data-commentator="Magen Avraham" data-order="9"></i><i data-commentator="Ba'er Hetev" data-order="11"></i><i data-commentator="Sha'arei Teshuvah" data-order="11"></i><i data-commentator="Mishnah Berurah" data-label="טז"></i>the congregation (responsa of the Rashba, siman 184)..</small>
